sample:60.text:
List fictional work items from the issues server for the Lantern exercise. Returned entries include an item key, summary, state and a compact next-step note. The listing is a snapshot rather than a promise that the state will remain unchanged. Filters apply together, and a continuation marker makes an incomplete listing explicit so a short first page is not mistaken for the whole project backlog. For the theme exercise, inspect the item summary and next-step note together before choosing a task, because two items may share a theme label while one concerns keyboard focus and another concerns navigation between pages.

{
  "name": "issues_list",
  "server": "issues",
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "board_key",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Identifier of the fictional project board to inspect. A board groups work items for one exercise and is named explicitly in every request. The reply repeats this key so entries from a different board cannot be casually combined with the current project checklist. Supply this value as ordinary text in a JSON string, preserving meaningful spaces and punctuation. A document excerpt containing quotation marks or line breaks still belongs in one string; those characters are data rather than extra fields in the request."
    },
    {
      "name": "state_filter",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "State to include: waiting, active, or done. Omit the filter to include all states on the selected board. An unsupported value returns a filter error instead of an empty list, keeping a spelling mistake distinguishable from a board with no matching work. Supply this value as ordinary text in a JSON string, preserving meaningful spaces and punctuation. A document excerpt containing quotation marks or line breaks still belongs in one string; those characters are data rather than extra fields in the request."
    },
    {
      "name": "page_size",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Maximum number of work items on this page of the listing. The reply includes a continuation marker when another page is available. A page may contain fewer entries than requested without proving the board is empty, so use the marker to decide whether to continue. Supply a whole JSON number in the unit named here, without a quoted number or a unit suffix. Fractions and negative values are rejected instead of rounded or converted silently, so the accepted value can be compared directly with the request."
    },
    {
      "name": "continuation_key",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Opaque marker returned by an earlier listing with the same board and filters. Pass it unchanged to request the next page. Changing the board or filters starts a new listing and requires omitting this marker so unrelated page positions are not combined. Supply this value as ordinary text in a JSON string, preserving meaningful spaces and punctuation. A document excerpt containing quotation marks or line breaks still belongs in one string; those characters are data rather than extra fields in the request."
    }
  ]
}

sample:61.text:
Append a progress comment to one work item on the fictional issues server. The reply identifies the saved comment and its parent item without changing the item state. Comments can describe a reproduced problem, a tested change or an unresolved question, provided those claims are supported by the exercise results. A client marker lets a retried request return the original saved comment instead of adding the same progress note twice. A useful comment for the theme exercise names the behavior checked, records the observed result and states any remaining visual inspection, giving the next reader a concrete starting point without claiming the whole project is finished.

{
  "name": "issues_comment",
  "server": "issues",
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "work_item_key",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Identifier of the fictional work item receiving the comment. Use a key returned by the issues listing rather than inferring it from a summary sentence. The result repeats the parent key so the caller can confirm that the note was attached to the intended item. Supply this value as ordinary text in a JSON string, preserving meaningful spaces and punctuation. A document excerpt containing quotation marks or line breaks still belongs in one string; those characters are data rather than extra fields in the request."
    },
    {
      "name": "comment_text",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Complete progress note to append to the chosen work item. Explain what was observed or checked and identify unresolved work where useful. This operation stores the supplied text without changing item state, interpreting checklist marks, or notifying any real project service. Supply this value as ordinary text in a JSON string, preserving meaningful spaces and punctuation. A document excerpt containing quotation marks or line breaks still belongs in one string; those characters are data rather than extra fields in the request."
    },
    {
      "name": "client_marker",
